| Comment: ============================================================
| Comment: MyDFIR Unauthorized Successful RDP Login Detection
| Comment: ============================================================
| Comment: Purpose       : Detect successful interactive RDP-style logons
| Comment:                 (EventCode 4624, Logon Types 7 and 10) that
| Comment:                 originate from outside the authorized corporate
| Comment:                 IP range. Fires the Shuffle SOAR webhook so
| Comment:                 the analyst can choose to disable the user.
| Comment: Author        : Vibhav Chennamadhava
| Comment: Date created  : 2026-06-10
| Comment: Splunk version: 9.x (Enterprise free trial)
| Comment: Index         : mydfir-ad
| Comment: Alert name    : MyDFIR-Unauthorized-Successful-Login-RDP
| Comment: Schedule      : * * * * *  (every minute, last 60 minutes)
| Comment: Trigger       : number of results > 0
| Comment: Throttle      : 24h per Source_Network_Address
| Comment: Trigger action: Webhook -> Shuffle SOAR workflow
| Comment: MITRE ATT&CK  : T1078 Valid Accounts, T1021.001 RDP
| Comment: ============================================================
| Comment: Filter rationale:
| Comment:   EventCode=4624            : successful logon
| Comment:   Logon_Type=7              : unlock / reconnected RDP session
| Comment:   Logon_Type=10             : RemoteInteractive (RDP establish)
| Comment:   Source_Network_Address=*  : must have a remote source set
| Comment:   != "-"                    : strip Windows local-logon sentinel
| Comment:   != 40.*                   : strip authorized corporate IPs
| Comment: ============================================================

index=mydfir-ad EventCode=4624
(Logon_Type=7 OR Logon_Type=10)
Source_Network_Address=*
Source_Network_Address!="-"
Source_Network_Address!=40.*
| stats count by _time, ComputerName, Source_Network_Address, user, Logon_Type
| sort -_time
